{"name":"Eagle","hex":"#a26c36","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Eagle","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The Apollo Lunar Module of Apollo 11."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname transferred from the nickname, from the name of the bird as a byname. See eagle.","Any of a number of rivers in the United States and Canada."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Eagle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Eagle","blocks":[{"text":"Eagle is the common name for certain large predatory birds of prey within the family of the Accipitridae. While on a genetic level, only the subfamily Aquilinae comprises \"true eagles\", many other species are commonly referred to as eagles, such as the bald eagle, and the term generally carries no taxonomic weight. Most of the 68 species of eagles are from Eurasia and Africa. Outside this area, just 14 species can be found—two in North America, nine in Central and South America, and three in Australia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Eagles_together.jpg/330px-Eagles_together.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eagle","wikidata":"Q2092297"},{"title":"Eagle (heraldry)","blocks":[{"text":"The eagle is used in heraldry as a charge, as a supporter, and as a crest. Heraldic eagles can be found throughout world history like in the Achaemenid Empire or in the present Republic of Indonesia. The European post-classical symbolism of the heraldic eagle is connected with the Roman Empire on one hand, and with Saint John the Evangelist on the other."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Str%C3%B6hl_Heraldischer_Atlas_t09_3.jpg/330px-Str%C3%B6hl_Heraldischer_Atlas_t09_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eagle_(heraldry)","wikidata":"Q358148"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/04/Old_Abe%2C_the_live_war_eagle_of_Wisconsin%2C_from_the_Centennial.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/04/Old_Abe%2C_the_live_war_eagle_of_Wisconsin%2C_from_the_Centennial.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"An Eagle named in honor of Abraham Lincoln and was the mascot of 8th Wisconsin Infantry Regiment, at the time of the U.S. Centennial","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOld_Abe%2C_the_live_war_eagle_of_Wisconsin%2C_from_the_Centennial.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/8f/Martial_Eagle_in_Namibia.jpg/500px-Martial_Eagle_in_Namibia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/8f/Martial_Eagle_in_Namibia.jpg/500px-Martial_Eagle_in_Namibia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Martial eagle in Namibia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMartial_Eagle_in_Namibia.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Pithecophaga_jefferyi.jpg/330px-Pithecophaga_jefferyi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Pithecophaga_jefferyi.jpg/330px-Pithecophaga_jefferyi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Philippine eagle (Pithecophaga jefferyi) in Southern Philippines","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APithecophaga_jefferyi.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/WedgetailEagleCarrion.jpg/500px-WedgetailEagleCarrion.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/WedgetailEagleCarrion.jpg/500px-WedgetailEagl